    "items": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Wherefore, Job, I pray thee, hear my speeches,",
          "And hearken to all my words."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Behold, now I have opened my mouth,",
          "My tongue hath spoken in my mouth."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My words shall be of the uprightness of my heart:",
          "And my lips shall utter knowledge clearly."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Spirit of God hath made me,",
          "And the breath of the Almighty hath given me life."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If thou canst answer me,",
          "Set thy words in order before me, stand up."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Behold, I am according to thy wish in God's stead:",
          "I also am formed out of the clay."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Behold, my terror shall not make thee afraid,",
          "Neither shall my hand be heavy upon thee."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Surely thou hast spoken in mine hearing,",
          "And I have heard the voice of thy words, saying,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I am clean without transgression,",
          "I am innocent; neither is there iniquity in me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Behold, he findeth occasions against me,",
          "He counteth me for his enemy,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He putteth my feet in the stocks,",
          "He marketh all my paths."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Behold, in this thou art not just: I will answer thee,",
          "that God is greater than man."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Why dost thou strive against him?",
          "For he giveth not account of any of his matters."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For God speaketh once,",
          "Yea twice, yet man perceiveth it not."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "In a dream, in a vision of the night,",
          "When deep sleep falleth upon men,",
          "In slumberings upon the bed;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then he openeth the ears of men,",
          "And sealeth their instruction,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "That he may withdraw man from his purpose,",
          "And hide pride from man."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He keepeth back his soul from the pit,",
          "And his life from perishing by the sword."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He is chastened also with pain upon his bed,",
          "And the multitude of his bones with strong pain:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "So that his life abhorreth bread,",
          "And his soul dainty meat."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "His flesh is consumed away, that it cannot be seen;",
          "And his bones that were not seen stick out."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Yea, his soul draweth near unto the grave,",
          "And his life to the destroyers."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If there be a messenger with him,",
          "An interpreter, one among a thousand,",
          "To shew unto man his uprightness:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then he is gracious unto him, and saith,",
          "Deliver him from going down to the pit:",
          "I have found a ransom."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "His flesh shall be fresher than a child's:",
          "He shall return to the days of his youth:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He shall pray unto God, and he will be favourable unto him:",
          "And he shall see his face with joy:",
          "For he will render unto man his righteousness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He looketh upon men, and if any say,",
          "I have sinned, and perverted that which was right,",
          "And it profited me not;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He will deliver his soul from going into the pit,",
          "And his life shall see the light."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Lo, all these things worketh God",
          "Oftentimes with man,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "To bring back his soul from the pit,",
          "To be enlightened with the light of the living."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          31
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Mark well, O Job, hearken unto me:",
          "Hold thy peace, and I will speak."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          32
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If thou hast any thing to say, answer me:",
          "Speak, for I desire to justify thee."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          33
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If not, hearken unto me:",
          "Hold thy peace, and I shall teach thee wisdom."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      }
    ]
  },
